{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The user is asking me to calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. using two data sources:\n1. https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv - farmers markets data\n2. https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv - census data\n\nAccording to the AGENTS.md file, I need to:\n1. Orient first - check semantic models and existing aliases\n2. Never state numbers I didn't obtain from xorq_select\n3. Ingest sources as their own aliases first\n4. Compose metrics as needed\n5. Verify all values with xorq_verify\n\nThe catalog path should be `.xorq/catalog` by default.\n\nLet me start by:\n1. Checking if semantic models exist\n2. Checking if aliases already exist for these datasets\n3. If not, I'll need to ingest both CSVs\n4. Then calculate the metric: (total farmers markets / total residents) * 100,000\n5. Verify the result"}}
