esponseId":"msg_011Ce78YLk1EcCj3ET8yPqcR","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KgxqqkozupfXKTrGGHnDwx","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"state_abbr\",\"farmers_markets\",\"csa_programs\",\"farm_stands\",\"snap_ebt_markets\",\"snap_ebt_pct\",\"organic_vendor_markets\",\"organic_pct\",\"markets_with_website\",\"website_pct\"\n\"California\",\"CA\",647,95,223,100,15.5,114,17.6,246,38.0\n\"New York\",\"NY\",555,156,272,41,7.4,45,8.1,283,51.0\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\",426,102,886,18,4.2,43,10.1,226,53.1\n\"Minnesota\",\"MN\",390,62,80,101,25.9,14,3.6,148,37.9\n\"Illinois\",\"IL\",370,64,713,29,7.8,42,11.4,155,41.9\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915408836},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_016gThn6NDmAxvgjEweiUfNx","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915408836},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! So:\n- Total US population (POPESTIMATE2025): 341,784,857\n- I need to sum up all farmers_markets from the farmers-markets table\n- Then calculate: (total_farmers_markets / 341,784,857) * 100,000\n\nLet me get the total farmers markets first.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DEZACf3SjXZQ5CkYRSpUMD","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers-markets","compose":"source.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":197,"cacheRead":16884,"cacheWrite":634,"totalTokens":17729,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.000985,"cacheRead":0.0016884,"cacheWrite":0.0007925,"total":0.0034799},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":79},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915408837,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78YhdcHnmGyG9KrAWKy","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01DEZACf3SjXZQ5CkYRSpUMD","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_farmers_markets\"\n7944\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915411975},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- Total US population: 341,784,857\n\nSo the calculation is:\n(7944 / 341784857) * 100000 = 2.3237...\n\nLet me now create a composed metric that joins these two values and calculates the per capita rate. According to the skill docs, I should do this as a build script that reads both sources and joins them, rather than composing.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0164QvjHKP92rQ4wTtPBivCy","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets and population\nfact_total = fact.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\nref_us = ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\").select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and calculate per capita rate\nexpr = (\n    fact_total.join(ref_us, fact_total.k == ref_us.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=fact_total.total_farmers_markets / ref_us.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":671,"cacheRead":17518,"cacheWrite":247,"totalTokens":18448,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0033550000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0017518000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00030875,"total":0.005427550000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":110},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915411975,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78YxV5MgCnbfGFqWz3F","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0164QvjHKP92rQ4wTtPBivCy","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1224 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915418824},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to build and add this to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KF5mbqczT8TiuBKJ3qnkNX","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-96-fq4jdyoh && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_metric.txt && cat /tmp/bp_metric.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":147,"cacheRead":17765,"cacheWrite":713,"totalTokens":18638,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0007350000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017765,"cacheWrite":0.00089125,"total":0.0034157500000000004},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":17},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915418824,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78ZTfFVENEbwaTCRnyr","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01KF5mbqczT8TiuBKJ3qnkNX","toolName":"bash","cont